13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434908 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1069 "q-114129" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1071 "![](images/a4/a493b0c356b7088479ec6c80afff94eb5e39fd8b31d14b771076b9a9ab37ddc1.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠AOD={170}^{∘}$ and $m∠BOD={130}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠AOC.$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1072 #uuid "d2a2e76f-a9f4-53a0-a562-a0ade38c838f" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434930 1074 "The measure of $∠AOB$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AOD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BOD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠AOB={170}^{∘}-{130}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/12/12431bb2f66402469571c49ac5637376f89e54265748fa88b3a6450c14bd7bce.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠AOC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434906 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1069 "q-150761" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1071 "![](images/39/39e491930076760f06a77929e4264d41ba3f921db918fb34dd49772036ad09d5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠QOS.$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1072 #uuid "d2f7aabf-f781-5516-8215-5f6f4e267c7c" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434931 1074 "![](images/53/537b98b49691a55102fd5c1d06f6635f770118113b3535e8c1238f169b2e4dfb.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠QOR$ and $∠ROS$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OR}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QOS & =m∠QOR+m∠ROS \\\\  & ={79}^{∘}+{41}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434914 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1069 "q-171821" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1071 "![](images/89/89c36c6195b98d333a7fedaf2bd2fe72b8c7b334aa92b85a5cc0ba1fc1145897.png)\n\nSince the measure of $∠BAD$ in the diagram above is ${85}^{∘},$ the angle $x$ must be equal to{{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1072 #uuid "d7d3aa87-356e-5bc2-8e85-8a227cbc986a" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434932 1074 "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={85}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}={45}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434909 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1069 "q-53141" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1071 "![](images/d3/d378eeecb9b30f1f76fb54c4279e94b0f469a776c7d774067f100697df7c7c4c.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠BOD.$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1072 #uuid "eda042a4-74d7-5136-ac0b-5b4db6d8b88f" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true] [17592186434933 1074 "![](images/17/17922d1ffef1dcd8bc798c8ffb8fe113a7e2e57cacc234641c84f59bbbcf6bbd.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OC}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & =m∠BOC+m∠COD \\\\  & ={52}^{∘}+{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ={102}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534746 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-060ae832-5075-56da-82fc-17a5809b5c48" 17592186434835 "answer-0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" 17592186434836 "answer-0c80eb4b-c4d6-5e5b-a19d-efe4a9b59e2f" 17592186434837 "answer-0cc3b37d-ee9e-561a-a603-10bed87792b9" 17592186434838 "answer-0e1cb4a0-7539-5215-901a-94090333335f" 17592186434839 "answer-0fd9acdd-9fd8-534e-ae92-2b533b6f1435" 17592186434840 "answer-11459e5c-dc18-5229-9996-832a86ce21b0" 17592186434841 "answer-130c6f21-6857-55ea-88a0-c147a7f849e4" 17592186434842 "answer-15e2a51e-6919-53ef-a340-c777e0278602" 17592186434843 "answer-1b2a3aad-85e3-5fb4-829b-3d11835d963a" 17592186434844 "answer-2014ad3b-af18-5cbf-9a7b-23ff3020c880" 17592186434845 "answer-20cde8dc-5569-53b9-ad42-37ced8ac948b" 17592186434846 "answer-24a6d6cf-caaa-5dcd-82d3-6c83523c1ae1" 17592186434847 "answer-28add8c4-ec45-5d93-a2b1-5b96bdf87160" 17592186434848 "answer-3043ced3-a2ab-50d1-b509-fcfa0dbf92a9" 17592186434849 "answer-3f5a9165-7b2a-5021-bcf0-8c1ec910418c" 17592186434850 "answer-48fdf3b5-2057-594f-84e9-26ee50f9ff83" 17592186434851 "answer-4a00bb7b-b835-5b61-b907-46193558bba4" 17592186434852 "answer-4c17bb3b-c189-555d-9e82-95710843f835" 17592186434853 "answer-4d991493-389d-5e33-97a3-6f9039a36093" 17592186434854 "answer-52965194-c33f-5a8e-88dd-e0042bd867a2" 17592186434855 "answer-57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" 17592186434856 "answer-58134ae4-42d3-52fa-8819-44f040d50e3b" 17592186434857 "answer-5ccc946c-9c73-58a2-8b98-f9f265dbc613" 17592186434858 "answer-5e411cc0-fdb3-5fff-b845-77c0cb3bd379" 17592186434859 "answer-5ed72a32-4f62-5d18-a45a-a67c35f83474" 17592186434860 "answer-5fdac38a-7cec-58d8-90c1-1e652d1486e2" 17592186434861 "answer-615b0b02-9899-5bec-bdae-86a42773e94e" 17592186434862 "answer-6b95ac2c-aed5-57a4-9c97-6